+# Privacy by Design Architecture Documentation
+
+**Project:** The Daily Grind Website  
+**Framework:** Cavoukian's 7 Foundational Principles of Privacy by Design, GDPR Art. 25, ISO/IEC 27701  
+
+---
+
+## 1. Proactive not Reactive; Preventative not Remedial
+- **Architecture:** Privacy mechanisms operate preventatively before any tracking can take place.
+- **Implementation:**
+  - Tracking query strings (`utm_*`, `fbclid`, `gclid`) are stripped immediately upon page initialization via `privacy.js`.
+  - Non-essential cookies and analytics scripts are blocked by default.
+  - CSP and Permissions-Policy disarm unauthorized data collection attempts at the browser level.
+
+## 2. Privacy as the Default Setting
+- **Architecture:** Zero action is required from the visitor to maintain their privacy.
+- **Implementation:**
+  - Opt-in consent model: Functional, analytics, and marketing categories default to `false`.
+  - Global Privacy Control (GPC) and Do Not Track (DNT) are natively detected via `navigator.globalPrivacyControl` and `navigator.doNotTrack`. When detected, all non-essential toggles are permanently locked to disabled.
+
+## 3. Privacy Embedded into Design
+- **Architecture:** Privacy is an integral element of the core functionality rather than an add-on.
+- **Implementation:**
+  - Forms are designed around **Data Minimization**:
+    - Newsletter requests only email (no telephone, name, address, or birthdate).
+    - Feedback requests minimal contact info with clear purpose and retention notices.
+  - Inputs use `autocomplete` and `spellcheck="false"` to prevent leakage to cloud-based spellcheckers or keyboards.
+
+## 4. Full Functionality — Positive-Sum, not Zero-Sum
+- **Architecture:** Legitimate business and user needs (ordering coffee, viewing seasonal menus, contacting customer support) thrive without sacrificing privacy.
+- **Implementation:**
+  - Users can browse menus, discover locations, and place orders without being forced to create an account or accept tracking cookies.
+
+## 5. End-to-End Security — Full Lifecycle Protection
+- **Architecture:** Data is protected from ingestion through storage to disposal.
+- **Implementation:**
+  - **Storage Hygiene:** No plaintext passwords, tokens, or PII stored in browser `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`.
+  - **Data Retention (TTL):** Consent preferences expire after 180 days; inquiries are purged after 30 days.
+  - **Secure Logout:** Logging out clears all client-side storage, expires cookies, and triggers the `Clear-Site-Data: "cache", "cookies", "storage"` header.
+  - **Security Headers:** Strict CSP, HSTS, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Referrer-Policy`, and COOP/COEP/CORP headers.
+
+## 6. Visibility and Transparency — Keep it Open
+- **Architecture:** Users are informed about what data is processed and why.
+- **Implementation:**
+  - Explicit purpose notices accompanying every form.
+  - Interactive "Third-Party Audit" modal and report documenting all external endpoints.
+  - Plain-language Privacy Policy accessible at `/privacy-policy`.
+
+## 7. Respect for User Privacy — Keep it User-Centric
+- **Architecture:** Puts the user in control of their personal information.
+- **Implementation:**
+  - **Right of Access & Portability:** Single-click "Export My Data" generates a clean JSON download of all stored device data.
+  - **Right to Erasure ("Forget Me"):** Single-click "Purge Stored Data" permanently removes all local preferences and cookies.
