+      <h1>Privacy Policy: Privacy by Design</h1>
+      <div class="effective-date">Effective Date: November 9, 2026 | ISO/IEC 27701 &amp; GDPR / CCPA Aligned</div>
+
+      <div class="highlight-box">
+        <strong>Our Foundational Commitment:</strong>
+        <p>The Daily Grind operates under the seven foundational principles of <em>Privacy by Design</em>. Privacy is not an afterthought, opt-out setting, or legal disclaimer—it is engineered directly into our website's HTML markup, scripts, and server infrastructure.</p>
+      </div>
+
+      <h2>1. Data Minimization Principles</h2>
+      <p>We adhere strictly to the principle of data minimization: we collect only personal data that is adequate, relevant, and strictly limited to what is necessary for our coffee roastery and ordering operations.</p>
+      <ul>
+        <li><strong>No Excessive Fields:</strong> Our newsletter requires only an email address. We never ask for your telephone number, physical address, birthdate, or demographic profile.</li>
+        <li><strong>No Covert Device Fingerprinting:</strong> We do not employ canvas fingerprinting, audio fingerprinting, or hardware profiling.</li>
+        <li><strong>URL Sanitization:</strong> Tracking identifiers (such as <code>utm_*</code>, <code>fbclid</code>, and <code>gclid</code>) are immediately stripped from page URLs upon arrival to prevent leakage across Referrer headers.</li>
+      </ul>
+
+      <h2>2. Third-Party Audits &amp; Inventory</h2>
+      <p>We routinely audit all external dependencies to ensure zero unauthorized third-party tracking scripts or surveillance networks touch your browser.</p>
+      <table>
+        <thead>
+          <tr>
+            <th>Provider / Origin</th>
+            <th>Resource Type</th>
+            <th>Purpose</th>
+            <th>Data Collected</th>
+            <th>Privacy Safeguards</th>
+          </tr>
+        </thead>
+        <tbody>
+          <tr>
+            <td><code>images.unsplash.com</code></td>
+            <td>Hero Image (CDN)</td>
+            <td>Visual ambiance</td>
+            <td>IP address (ephemeral CDN transit)</td>
+            <td><code>referrerpolicy="no-referrer"</code>, <code>crossorigin="anonymous"</code>, CSP restricted.</td>
+          </tr>
+          <tr>
+            <td>First-Party (The Daily Grind)</td>
+            <td>HTML, CSS, JS</td>
+            <td>Core site delivery</td>
+            <td>None (stateless)</td>
+            <td>Strict CSP, HSTS, Clear-Site-Data on logout.</td>
+          </tr>
+        </tbody>
+      </table>
+
+      <h2>3. Global Privacy Control (GPC) &amp; Do Not Track (DNT)</h2>
+      <p>We natively support and prioritize browser privacy signals: if you broadcast a <code>Sec-GPC: 1</code> (Global Privacy Control) or <code>DNT: 1</code> (Do Not Track) signal, all non-essential scripts, functional preferences, and telemetry are automatically disabled by default.</p>
+
+      <h2>4. Secure Data Handling &amp; Retention (TTL)</h2>
+      <p>All temporary data is subject to strict Time-To-Live (TTL) expiration schedules:</p>
+      <ul>
+        <li><strong>Session and Cart State:</strong> Kept in memory and discarded upon browser exit or when you click <a href="/logout">Logout</a>.</li>
+        <li><strong>Privacy Preferences:</strong> Retained in client local storage for a maximum of 180 days before re-prompting.</li>
+        <li><strong>Customer Inquiries:</strong> Retained for a maximum of 30 days to resolve your message, after which they are permanently deleted from customer service memory.</li>
+      </ul>
+
+      <h2>5. Security Headers &amp; Technical Safeguards</h2>
+      <p>Our server and markup implement industry-standard defense-in-depth protections:</p>
+      <ul>
+        <li><strong>Content-Security-Policy (CSP):</strong> Prohibits unauthorized script execution and restricts connections to approved origins.</li>
+        <li><strong>Permissions-Policy:</strong> Disables camera, microphone, geolocation, and FLoC/interest-cohort tracking APIs.</li>
+        <li><strong>X-Content-Type-Options:</strong> Enforces <code>nosniff</code> to prevent MIME-sniffing exploits.</li>
+        <li><strong>X-Frame-Options:</strong> Set to <code>DENY</code> to eliminate clickjacking vectors.</li>
+        <li><strong>Clear-Site-Data:</strong> Triggered upon logout to purge cached assets, cookies, and local storage on shared workstations.</li>
+      </ul>
+
+      <h2>6. Your Data Rights (GDPR &amp; CCPA)</h2>
+      <p>You have full ownership of any data associated with your interaction:</p>
+      <ul>
+        <li><strong>Right of Access &amp; Portability:</strong> You can download a complete JSON export of all data stored on this device by visiting our home page and clicking <em>Export My Data</em>.</li>
+        <li><strong>Right to Erasure ("Forget Me"):</strong> You can purge all local preferences, cookies, and cached data immediately via the <em>Purge Stored Data</em> button.</li>
+      </ul>
